WEBVTT

1
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:43.040
The fictional service case keeps the customer request in view.

2
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:59.040
An automated test asks the copilot for a policy-cited draft.

3
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:37.880
The selected case reference gives the draft its context.

4
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:47.880
The draft cites policy and flags the refund for supervisor review.

5
00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:55.640
The save skill checks the draft against the recorded team rules.

6
00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:09.000
The case keeps the draft ready for review.

7
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:15.600
The workflow stamps the record: AI draft, not sent.

8
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.880
The supervisor-review flag helps reviewers find the case.

9
00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:47.740
Reopen the fictional service case to review its reply.

10
00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:52.780
Edit mode opens the reply and review fields.

11
00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:59.780
An automated test types a reply with unsupported refund and compensation promises.

12
00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:06.220
Marking Ready to send starts the advisory review on save.

13
00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:16.500
Saving the reply starts its advisory policy check.

14
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:33.300
The workflow checks recorded phrases and amounts against the team rules.

15
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:42.980
The advisory check lists five policy problems for the reviewer.
